## Domain
Cross-tree reduction: the duplication audit (**#46**) + the **one-door build-failing
guards** that pin a converged capability so a second door can't silently reappear. The
existing guards are the template: `closure_guard` ("nothing manipulates schema/state
outside the algebra") and **#45** ("one `address → process` instantiation path"). For
THIS push you own **Stage 3** of the homoiconic unification.

## Now / next — homoiconic unification, Stage 3 (the guard; gated on `lang`'s Stage 2)
- [ ] **The one-instantiate guard** — a build-failing test asserting **exactly one
      function turns an entity (definer OR constructor) into a spec Value**, after `lang`
      collapses the N `build_X_value` builders into `instantiate` (Stage 2a). Model it on
      `closure_guard` / #45 (a sealed seam / single-`match` / grep-or-AST test). This is
      the generalization that keeps the unified face from re-forking.
- [ ] **Homoiconic-surface duplication audit (#46-scoped)** — sweep the
      definer ↔ constructor ↔ `to_value`/`from_value` ↔ `compile_reaction` surface for
      remaining multiplicity; spin off one consolidation per confirmed duplicate. Verify
      the Stage-1/2 collapses actually deleted the old paths (no dead `build_brs_value` /
      `compile_reaction_value` left behind).
- [ ] **Stretch** — generalize the one-door pattern into a small reusable
      architectural-invariant test helper (sealed-trait-one-impl / exhaustive-match /
      single-builder), so future convergences get a guard cheaply (`generative-core.md`
      §3).

## Verified audit findings (2026-06-09, read first-hand — refines unify's §1 table)
- **(A) 7 builder paths, not 5.** Capitalized-constructor dispatch = `eval_term_value`
  (`eval.rs:709`). *Entity door* (Stage 2a collapses): `build_composite_outer` (`:723`),
  `build_pure_spec`→`build_spec_value` (process/step, `:729`/`:735`→`:1117`),
  `build_reaction_value` (`:1202`), `build_protocol_outer` (`:743`). *Built-in*:
  `build_brs_value` (`"BRS"` string-match, `:768`/`:1354`). *Two DISTINCT doors* (decide
  with lang/unify whether they also funnel through `instantiate`): `build_native_spec`
  (wholesale native imports, `:777`) and `build_plain_map_value` (free-control fallback,
  `:1388` — **this is where missing `Reaction[…]`/`Pattern[…]` constructors currently
  mis-route**, so Stage 2b must intercept here).
- **(B) The Stage-2a crux (the headline).** `build_reaction_value` returns a **runnable**
  `Foreign(FOREIGN_RULE, Rule)`; the node builders return **data** spec-maps
  `{_type,address,config,inputs,outputs}`. The §7 quote/eval split resolves the
  inconsistency: a constructor should produce **DATA (= quote of the definer)**, the
  runnable produced by **eval** (`compile_reaction = eval∘quote`, Stage 1b). So the
  collapse target is *one instantiate → quote-consistent data*, with eval as the separate
  2nd rung. The reaction builder is the lone odd-one-out conflating quote+eval.
- **(C) Dismissed false positive (verified).** `reaction.rs::Pattern::{to_value,from_value}`
  (lossless **pattern-as-data**, keeps holes via `_pat` tags) vs
  `assembly.rs::{to_value,from_value}` (**ground-state rendering**, errors on holes) are
  DISTINCT ops that coexist *by design* (`reaction.rs:380`) — NOT a duplicate; no
  consolidation. (Minor clarity nit, not a task: assembly's pair could be named
  `to_ground_value`/`from_ground_value` to retire the shared-name confusion.)
- **Offer to lang:** the no-wildcard **exhaustiveness witness** mechanism for the Stage-1a
  round-trip test — makes "total over all variants" build-FAILING (a new `Expr` variant
  can't compile until covered), properly pinning invariant #2 instead of sample-testing it.

## Coordinate
Your guards are NEW test files → monotone, go. But a one-door guard CONSTRAINS everyone
(it can fail their `cargo test`) → before landing a guard that could break in-flight
work, read the board + drop a `note` so `lang`/others rebuild against it (CALM /
ROSTER §regimes). Pair with `lang` on what the canonical one door actually is; with
`unify` on whether a found duplicate is essential (a logged conservative extension) or
accidental (delete it).

